@startuml mf-03-cancel-delete
' SRS Section II.1.2.3 — Main Workflow: Cancel & Delete
' Deleting a cargo is the operator-facing action; cancelling its transport task
' is the consequence. The pickup-lane release that follows is performed by the
' next dispatch flush, not inside the delete request.
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-03-cancel-delete.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

title Cancel & Delete

|#FAFAFA|Admin / Operator|
|#FFFFFF|WES|
|#F2F2F2|FMS (openTCS)|
|#F2F2F2|AGV|

|Admin / Operator|
start
:Request cargo deletion;

|WES|
if (Cargo exists?) then (No)
  :Reject:\n"Cargo not found";
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Look up the linked\ntransport task;
if (Task is DELIVERING?) then (Yes)
  :Reject (MSG-24): the AGV is\nalready carrying this item\nto its destination;
  note right
    The cargo is NOT deleted.
    This is the ONLY guard
    that blocks deletion.
  end note
  stop
else (No, or no\ntask at all)
endif
if (Task is PICKING_UP?) then (Yes)
  |FMS (openTCS)|
  :Withdraw the pick-up transport\norder (graceful; WES does\nNOT wait for confirmation);
  |AGV|
  :Finish the movement\ncurrently being executed,\nthen stop driving\nto the source point;
  |WES|
else (No)
endif
if (Task cancellable?\nCREATED / READY_TO_ASSIGN\n/ BLOCKED / PICKING_UP) then (Yes)
  :Stamp the cancellation\ntimestamp;
  :Task -> CANCELLED\n(reason: cargo deleted);
  :Raise the\nstatus-changed event;
else (No)
  :No task update - the task\nis already in a terminal state\n(DELIVERY_COMPLETED /\nFAILED / CANCELLED);
endif
:Remove the cargo from\nthe system (soft delete);
:Confirm the deletion\nto the operator;
#CDE9CD:Next dispatch flush -\n1.5 s after the\nstatus-changed event;
note right
  The deleted cargo has left its pickup
  lane, so it no longer blocks anything
  behind it. The AGV freed by the
  cancellation is reconsidered in the
  same flush.
end note
#CDE9CD:Release Engine re-evaluates\nthe lanes against the\nouter-before-inner rule (BR-10);
if (Any task still BLOCKED\nbehind the deleted cargo\nin the same lane?) then (Yes)
  #CDE9CD:Clear the block reason;\nTask -> READY_TO_ASSIGN;
  #CDE9CD:Assignment Engine (Hungarian)\nmatches it with a free vehicle\nand issues its pick-up order;
  |FMS (openTCS)|
  :Route that vehicle\ninto the freed lane;
  |AGV|
  :Drive in and collect\nthe next cargo;
  |WES|
else (No)
  #CDE9CD:Nothing to release\nin this lane;
endif
stop

legend bottom
|<#7ACFF4>    | Handled synchronously, inside the operator's delete request |
|<#CDE9CD>    | Pickup-lane release - performed by the next dispatch flush |
endlegend

@enduml
